Neha,

Apologies for the delay on this, I was looking for it in the wrong folder and
then the week went. Forwarding the whole chain for VAR-008 as you asked. I have
not trimmed anything because you said you want the full trail for the evidence
folder, so it is long and the bottom half is Sales Ops and reports and not much
use to you. The three mails in the middle are the ones that matter.

Summary, as per my earlier mail dated 11-Mar.

1. LP_DAILY_SALES failed on the night of Saturday 14-Feb-2026 and was
resubmitted by hand. That re-run is session SESS_884012. Nothing else in
February was resubmitted.

2. IKM Oracle Control Append does not merge. There is no update branch on that
mapping at all, so everything the incremental predicate returned went in a
second time. The whole of the 14/02/26 night is in the fact twice.

3. Value of the duplicated sales is INR 2,94,10,000, that is 2.9 Cr. It sat
inside the February figures for three weeks before anybody tied the month back.

4. Reconciliation item closed on 02-Apr-2026. The batch id guard went in with
R2026.07 on 08-Jul-2026, so a deliberate re-run of the same batch is stopped
now.

5. One thing you will ask for and I do not have. There is no mail from February
saying the run had failed. It failed, I resubmitted it, the plan completed, and
that was the end of it as far as anybody knew until Vikram's mail on the 6th.
That gap is not a process I can point at, it is simply that a resubmit was
normal and nobody logged it.

If you want the Control-M history for the month I can export it, tell me which
format you want it in.

